ocratic ticket alongside several independents. No general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on the state's fundamentals. Oklahoma leans about 17 points Republican at the presidential level, and every major race rater — Cook, Sabato, DDHQ, Silver Bulletin and others — rates the contest Solid or Safe Republican. Prediction markets give Munson roughly a 7-8% chance. Mazzei's contested primary and Munson's argument that Oklahomans are ready for change give Democrats a talking point, but the structural environment strongly favors Republicans, and a Trump rally in Durant underscores the nationalized Republican advantage heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -13.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0251, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0363, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0321, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -14.0}]}